  "numerical_contract": {
    "integrator": "Implicit midpoint, damped Newton, 26 MNA variables; hot DC operating-point initialization. Midpoint avoids backward-Euler damping of high-Q IF tanks.",
    "steps": "48/96/192 steps per carrier cycle; default 96. Coupling-leakage fixtures require 192 because their nonlinear audio response amplifies carrier-step error.",
    "statistics": "Final four modulation periods, using full-rate states. The finite arrival window includes settling; no steady-state sensitivity claim.",
    "display": "One sample per carrier cycle; carrier amplitudes are calculated before display decimation.",
    "reference": "B-minus, not chassis. DC source 90\u2013130 V.",
    "scope": "Joint electrical IF-to-speaker response; electrical speaker equivalent, no acoustic calibration.",
    "convergence": "Damped Newton with up to four step subdivisions on failure; strict signal-node residuals, 1 nA supply-node stopping allowance for fine-step roundoff, overall accepted normalized residual <10 nA. Leakage equilibrium uses conductance continuation."
  }
